# Muxel secrets.
#
# The deploy flow reads this file to work out what to ask for, so it lists only
# what a deployment cannot start without. Copy it to .dev.vars for local
# development. Never commit real values: .dev.vars is ignored by git for that
# reason.
#
# One box, on purpose. Everything else this deployment can be given — a console
# bot in Telegram, a key for a model from another provider, live web search,
# reading a document as data — is added afterwards, from the Worker's own
# Settings, Variables and Secrets. A form of empty boxes at the very first step
# reads as work to do before anything happens, and it is not.

# The key that signs you into the web console at app.muxel.site.
#
# Make one up, at least 16 characters, and keep it where you keep passwords.
# Your deployment answers on a public address, so this key is the whole lock on
# it. Forgetting it costs nothing: change CONSOLE_KEY in the Worker's settings
# and the new one works, which also ends every session the old one opened.
#
# If you would rather drive the console from Telegram instead, or as well, add
# ADMIN_BOT_TOKEN and OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID in Settings afterwards; the setup page
# says how. Either door on its own is enough.
CONSOLE_KEY=
